# Code owners for `grover-tax`.
#
# Routes review of methodology-critical paths to the maintainer set defined
# in `docs/rfcs/RFC-0014-governance.md` §"CODEOWNERS". For `v0.1` the
# maintainer set is one (`@AbdelStark`); adding maintainers requires an
# RFC-0014 update.
#
# CODEOWNERS rules cascade in declaration order — the LAST matching pattern
# wins. The catch-all on the first line therefore stands as the default; the
# more specific paths below override it (which today happens to be a no-op,
# but the explicit pinning is intentional: it makes the methodology
# boundaries auditable from this file alone, and it keeps the routing
# correct if additional maintainers join the catch-all later).

*                              @AbdelStark

# Workload pin: the contract that ties this benchmark to upstream at a
# specific commit (RFC-0001).
WORKLOAD.md                    @AbdelStark

# Fixtures and the toolchain lock: the inputs the benchmark consumes
# (RFC-0002, RFC-0012).
fixtures/                      @AbdelStark
versions.lock                  @AbdelStark

# Specification corpus and RFCs: the methodology itself.
docs/spec/                     @AbdelStark
docs/spec/templates/           @AbdelStark
docs/rfcs/                     @AbdelStark

# SP1 patch surface: bounded by the line budget in RFC-0006.
sp1-side-patches/              @AbdelStark

# Reporting: `analyze.py` produces RESULTS.md (RFC-0011).
analyze.py                     @AbdelStark

# CI workflows: gate every other rule.
.github/workflows/             @AbdelStark
